<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
/E (Students frequently report concerns regarding food quality, hygiene, inconsistent menus, insufficient portions, and cleanliness of dining areas. These complaints are usually sent through emails or messaging groups, making them difficult to monitor. Without proper documentation and follow-up, similar complaints continue to arise every semester.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
/E (Irregular water supply, poor drinking water quality, Wi-Fi outages, electrical failures, and malfunctioning common facilities disrupt students' daily lives. Since complaints are scattered across different communication channels, authorities often lack a complete picture of recurring problems, leading to repeated reporting of the same issues without long-term solutions.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
