<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 174 0 R
/E (Students also experience delays related to faculty advisors, department offices, scholarships, examination processes, certificates, and approvals. Finding the appropriate authority itself can be confusing, and students often have to send multiple reminder emails or personally visit offices just to receive an update on their request.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 174 0 R
/E (Students regularly encounter issues such as damaged roads, inadequate street lighting, overflowing dustbins, malfunctioning drinking water stations, poorly maintained sports facilities, and unhygienic common spaces. Since there is no centralized record of infrastructure-related complaints, maintenance becomes reactive rather than proactive, affecting the overall campus environment.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 174 0 R
/E (Students occasionally face delays or difficulties with campus medical facilities, counseling appointments, ambulance services, accessibility support, and other student welfare services. With complaints handled through multiple communication channels, there is limited visibility into response times and resolution progress. The lack of systematic tracking makes it difficult for authorities to identify recurring service gaps and improve the quality of support for students.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
